<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/docs" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 font-medium transition-colors group">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 transform group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path></svg>
      Back to Documentation
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12">
    <!-- Sidebar Partial -->

    <!-- Main Content -->
     <main class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-12 space-y-12">
      <!-- Header Section -->
      <div class="relative">
        <div class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-indigo-600 rounded-lg blur opacity-25"></div>
        <div class="relative">
          <h1 class="text-5xl font-extrabold text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-400 via-indigo-400 to-purple-400 mb-4 tracking-tight">Queue Management</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
            Scalable, distributed background job processing for SoliDB.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview Section -->
      <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-indigo-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10"></path></svg>
              Overview
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-8 text-gray-300 space-y-4 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              SoliDB provides a built-in, distributed queue system backed by the database itself. Jobs are stored as documents in the <code class="text-indigo-400">_jobs</code> collection, ensuring persistence and reliability.
            </p>
            <p>
              Key features include:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
              <li><strong>Distributed Workers</strong>: Every node in a SoliDB cluster runs background workers that automatically pick up and execute jobs.</li>
              <li><strong>Optimistic Locking</strong>: Uses SoliDB's revision check (<code class="bg-gray-800 px-1 rounded">_rev</code>) to ensure that a job is executed by exactly one worker, even in a large cluster.</li>
              <li><strong>Priorities & Retries</strong>: Jobs support priority levels and automatic retries with exponential backoff.</li>
              <li><strong>Per-queue settings</strong>: Each queue can be <strong>paused</strong> (workers stop claiming new jobs while running ones finish), capped to a maximum <strong>concurrency</strong>, and given a <strong>default priority</strong> applied to jobs enqueued without an explicit one. Settings live in the <code class="text-indigo-400">_queue_config</code> collection and are purely additive — a queue with no config row keeps the historical behavior (running, unlimited concurrency, priority 0).</li>
              <li><strong>Two execution targets</strong>:
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-6 mt-2">
                  <li><strong>Script</strong> — set <code class="text-indigo-400">script</code> to run a server-side Lua script close to your data.</li>
                  <li><strong>Webhook</strong> — set <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_url</code> to have the worker POST the job's <code class="text-indigo-400">params</code> directly to an external URL, with an optional HMAC-signed <code class="text-indigo-400">X-Webhook-Signature</code> header. No script registration needed.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- API Reference Section -->
      <section id="api" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-blue-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 9l3 3-3 3m5 0h3M5 20h14a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
              API Reference
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="divide-y divide-white/5">
            
            <!-- Enqueue -->
            <div class="p-6 hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-green-500/20 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">POST</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/queues/:queue/enqueue</code>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Enqueue a new job. <strong class="text-gray-300">Exactly one</strong> of <code class="text-indigo-400">script</code> or <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_url</code> must be set — they select between Lua-script execution and outbound-HTTP execution respectively.</p>

               <div class="mb-4">
                 <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Request Body</h4>
                 <div class="bg-gray-950/50 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-white/5">
                   <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
                     <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300 font-bold border-b border-white/5">
                       <tr><th class="p-3">Field</th><th class="p-3">Type</th><th class="p-3">Description</th></tr>
                     </thead>
                     <tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/5">
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">script</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">string</td><td class="p-3">Path/name of the Lua script to execute. <em>Mutually exclusive with <code>webhook_url</code>.</em></td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">webhook_url</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">string</td><td class="p-3">When set, the worker POSTs <code>params</code> (as JSON) to this URL instead of running a script. Accepts <code>callback_url</code> as an alias.</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">webhook_secret</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">string</td><td class="p-3">Per-job HMAC-SHA256 key for signing the body via <code>X-Webhook-Signature</code>. Falls back to <code>SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> / <code>SOLI_JOBS_SECRET</code> env vars when omitted.</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">webhook_headers</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">object</td><td class="p-3">Extra HTTP headers attached to the outbound webhook request.</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">params</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">object</td><td class="p-3">JSON arguments passed to the script, or POSTed as the body for webhook jobs. Accepts <code>args</code> as an alias.</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">priority</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">integer</td><td class="p-3">Higher values execute first. When omitted, falls back to the queue's configured <code>default_priority</code> (0 if the queue has no config row).</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">max_retries</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">integer</td><td class="p-3">Max attempts on failure (exponential backoff between retries).</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">run_at</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">int | string</td><td class="p-3">Unix-seconds integer or RFC-3339 timestamp for delayed execution. Defaults to "now".</td></tr>
                     </tbody>
                   </table>
                 </div>
               </div>

               <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Example — Script target</h4>
               <div class="bg-gray-950/50 p-3 rounded border border-white/5 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 mb-3">
                 {"script": "send_email", "params": {"to": "user@example.com", "body": "Hello"}, "priority": 10}
               </div>

               <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Example — Webhook target</h4>
               <div class="bg-gray-950/50 p-3 rounded border border-white/5 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300">
                 {"webhook_url": "https://hooks.example.com/order", "params": {"order_id": 1234}, "webhook_secret": "s3cret", "webhook_headers": {"X-Source": "solidb"}}
               </div>

               <div class="mt-4 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-lg p-4 text-xs">
                 <p class="text-amber-200">
                   <strong>Webhook delivery contract:</strong> the worker POSTs <code class="text-amber-300">params</code> as JSON with
                   <code class="text-amber-300">Content-Type: application/json</code>,
                   <code class="text-amber-300">X-Webhook-Event: job</code>,
                   <code class="text-amber-300">X-Webhook-Delivery: &lt;job-id&gt;</code>, and (when a secret is available)
                   <code class="text-amber-300">X-Webhook-Signature</code> = lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256 of the body. Signing key lookup order: per-job <code class="text-amber-300">webhook_secret</code> → <code class="text-amber-300">SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> → <code class="text-amber-300">SOLI_JOBS_SECRET</code> → unsigned (see <a href="#configuration" class="underline hover:text-amber-100">Configuration</a>).
                   Any non-2xx response counts as failure and is retried per <code class="text-amber-300">max_retries</code>.
                 </p>
               </div>
            </div>

            <!-- List Queues -->
            <div class="p-6 hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-2">
                 <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500/20 text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">GET</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/queues</code>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Get statistics for all queues. Each entry includes per-job counts (<code>pending</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>completed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>total</code>) plus the queue's settings (<code>paused</code>, <code>concurrency</code>, <code>default_priority</code>). A queue that has been configured but has no jobs yet still appears in the list.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Update Queue Settings -->
            <div class="p-6 hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-yellow-500/20 text-yellow-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">PUT</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/queues/:queue</code>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Create or update a queue's settings. Fields are optional — omitted fields keep their current value (patch semantics), so you can flip a single setting. The queue need not have any jobs yet; this is how a queue gets pre-configured. The settings are upserted into the <code class="text-indigo-400">_queue_config</code> collection (keyed by queue name), and the full updated config is returned.</p>

               <div class="mb-4">
                 <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Request Body</h4>
                 <div class="bg-gray-950/50 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-white/5">
                   <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
                     <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300 font-bold border-b border-white/5">
                       <tr><th class="p-3">Field</th><th class="p-3">Type</th><th class="p-3">Description</th></tr>
                     </thead>
                     <tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/5">
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">paused</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">boolean</td><td class="p-3">When <code>true</code>, the worker claims no new jobs from this queue; already-running jobs finish, and pending jobs wait until the queue is resumed.</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">concurrency</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">integer</td><td class="p-3">Maximum jobs from this queue allowed to run at once. <code>0</code> means unlimited (the historical default).</td></tr>
                       <tr><td class="p-3 text-fuchsia-400 font-mono">default_priority</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">integer</td><td class="p-3">Priority assigned to jobs enqueued on this queue when the enqueue request omits an explicit <code>priority</code>. May be negative.</td></tr>
                     </tbody>
                   </table>
                 </div>
               </div>

               <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Example — Pause a queue and cap concurrency</h4>
               <div class="bg-gray-950/50 p-3 rounded border border-white/5 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300">
                 {"paused": true, "concurrency": 3, "default_priority": 5}
               </div>

               <div class="mt-4 bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/30 rounded-lg p-4 text-xs">
                 <p class="text-indigo-200">
                   <strong>Takes effect immediately:</strong> resuming a queue or raising its concurrency nudges the workers to re-check right away instead of waiting for the next poll.
                 </p>
               </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Lua Driver Section -->
      <section id="lua" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
             <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-purple-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 20l4-16m4 4l4 4-4 4M6 16l-4-4 4-4"></path></svg>
              Lua Driver
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">
              You can enqueue jobs directly from your application using the SoliDB Lua driver.
            </p>
            
            <div class="bg-gray-950/50 rounded-lg border border-white/5 p-4 overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-lua text-sm">-- Enqueue a job in the 'default' queue
db:queue("default"):enqueue("process_image", {
  image_id = "img_123",
  format = "webp"
})

-- With options
db:queue("emails"):enqueue("send_welcome", { user_id = "u1" }, {
  priority = 100,
  max_retries = 5
})</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Dashboard Section -->
      <section id="dashboard" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
             <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-emerald-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z"></path></svg>
              Dashboard
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 text-gray-300">
            <p class="mb-4">
              Monitor your queues visually using the dedicated <strong>Queues</strong> tab in the database dashboard.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
               <li>View pending, running, and failed job counts.</li>
               <li>Inspect job details and parameters.</li>
               <li>Cancel pending jobs.</li>
               <li>Manually enqueue jobs for testing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Cron Jobs Section -->
      <section id="cron" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
             <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-amber-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
              Cron Jobs (Schedules)
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-8 text-gray-300 space-y-6">
            <p>
              SoliDB supports scheduled jobs via cron expressions. Schedules are stored in the <code class="text-indigo-400">_cron_jobs</code> collection and are automatically managed by the cluster.
            </p>

            <div class="bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/30 rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="flex items-start">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-400 mt-0.5 mr-3 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <strong class="text-indigo-300">Cluster-Safe Execution:</strong>
                  <span class="text-gray-400"> SoliDB uses optimistic locking to ensure that even in a multi-node cluster, <strong>only one node</strong> will spawn a job for a given schedule tick.</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6">Cron Expression Format</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              SoliDB uses a 7-field cron expression format (including seconds and year):
            </p>
            <div class="bg-gray-950/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-white/5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto text-amber-400">
              sec min hour day month day_of_week year
            </div>
            
            <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
              <p>Examples:</p>
              <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4 text-gray-400 font-mono text-xs">
                <li><code class="text-amber-400">0 */5 * * * * *</code> - Every 5 minutes</li>
                <li><code class="text-amber-400">0 0 * * * * *</code> - Every hour</li>
                <li><code class="text-amber-400">0 0 0 * * * *</code> - Every day at midnight</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6">Job Identification</h3>
            <p>
              When a cron job spawns a regular job, the new job will contain a <code class="text-indigo-400">cron_job_id</code> field. In the Dashboard, these jobs are identified by a <span class="text-indigo-400 font-bold font-mono">clock icon</span>.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6">API Management</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 italic">Endpoints for managing schedules. The create/update bodies accept the same <code class="text-indigo-400">script</code> / <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_url</code> / <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_secret</code> / <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_headers</code> fields as the queue-enqueue endpoint — when a cron fires it spawns a job with whichever target was configured.</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-green-500/20 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">POST</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/cron</code>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-blue-500/20 text-blue-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">GET</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/cron</code>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-red-500/20 text-red-400 text-xs font-bold rounded">DELETE</span>
                <code class="text-gray-300">/_api/database/:db/cron/:id</code>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Configuration Section -->
      <section id="configuration" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
             <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-orange-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10.325 4.317c.426-1.756 2.924-1.756 3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 002.573 1.066c1.543-.94 3.31.826 2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 001.065 2.572c1.756.426 1.756 2.924 0 3.35a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.066 2.573c.94 1.543-.826 3.31-2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.572 1.065c-.426 1.756-2.924 1.756-3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.573-1.066c-1.543.94-3.31-.826-2.37-2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.065-2.572c-1.756-.426-1.756-2.924 0-3.35a1.724 1.724 0 001.066-2.573c-.94-1.543.826-3.31 2.37-2.37.996.608 2.296.07 2.572-1.065z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"></path></svg>
              Configuration
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
              Workers and webhook signing are configured globally via environment variables (either exported directly or loaded from a <code class="text-indigo-400 font-mono">.env</code> file).
            </p>
            <div class="bg-gray-950/50 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-white/5 mb-4">
              <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-400">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold">Variable</th>
                    <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold">Default</th>
                    <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold">Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 text-gray-300">
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono text-fuchsia-400">QUEUE_WORKERS</td>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono">4</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Number of concurrent job workers spawned per node.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono text-fuchsia-400">SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</td>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono text-gray-500">unset</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Default HMAC-SHA256 key used to sign webhook job &amp; trigger payloads via <code>X-Webhook-Signature</code>. Used when no per-job/per-trigger <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_secret</code> is supplied. When unset <strong>and</strong> no per-target secret is supplied, the signature header is omitted entirely.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono text-fuchsia-400">SOLI_JOBS_SECRET</td>
                    <td class="p-3 font-mono text-gray-500">unset</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Fallback key checked only if <code class="text-indigo-400">SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> is unset. Provided for migrating deployments that historically used this name; prefer <code class="text-indigo-400">SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> for new setups.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-950/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-white/5 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
               QUEUE_WORKERS=8 SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET=s3cret ./solidb-server ...
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-3">
              Secret-resolution order per outbound webhook: <code class="text-indigo-400">webhook_secret</code> field on the job/trigger → <code class="text-indigo-400">SOLI_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> → <code class="text-indigo-400">SOLI_JOBS_SECRET</code> → unsigned.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

     </main>
  </div>
</div>
